    "text": "> Computers often run several programs at the same time. So, source to destination delivery means delivery from a specific process on one computer to a specific process on the other. > Transport layer header include a service-point address(Port address) of source and destination. > A transport layer protocol can be either connectionless or connection-oriented. CTP ) Retroble > A connectionless transport layer treats each seSment’ as an independent packet. > Aconnection-oriented transport layer makes a connection with the transport layer at the destination machine first before delivering the packets. After all data 1s transferred, connection 1s terminated. > Like the data link layer, the transport layer may be responsible for flow and error control. However, flow and error control at this layer is performed end to end rather than across a single link.",
